WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.580
In this lesson, you will learn to play notes and melodies with the music blocks, using note numbers, beats and loops for rhythms.

2
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.290
In Scratch, notes have numbers.

3
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.120
60 is middle C.

4
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:22.330
Going up by 2 gives the next white key: 60 C, 62 D, 64 E, 65 F, 67 G, 69 A, 71 B, 72 high C.

5
00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.650
Play notes one after another to make a tune.

6
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.820
The order matters, just like any script!

7
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:34.320
A beat is a unit of time in music.

8
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.780
1 beat is a long note, 0.5 beats is quicker, 0.25 is very quick.

9
00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.480
Music repeats!

10
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.870
Use repeat to play a pattern again and again — that’s a rhythm or a riff.

11
00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.700
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:56.130
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
